{
  "rationale": "The plant separates perception (obstacle events) from motion commands, modeling the robot's open-loop pulse actions and sensor outcomes. The specification binds each perception outcome to a unique, progress-oriented controllable action, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed and rapid return to exploration. Rotations are preferred for side obstacles, backward motion is brief and only for front obstacles, and full_rotate is reserved for repeated blockages. The design ensures safety, steady coverage, and avoids oscillation or repeated identical actions.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model perception and motion as a single plant automaton with helper states for commit/recovery actions, ensuring all uncontrollable events are handled in every state.",
    "Specification automaton enforces unique controllable action per state, biases toward forward/random_walk in clear, uses rotate_clockwise for left obstacles, rotate_counterclockwise for right, and move_backward for front; full_rotate is only enabled after repeated blockages."
  ],
